  to operate in the country  we want to very much say thank you and  appreciation for  the shanghai government and the support  yung xi wang is the director of a group  at uc davis  studying china's transportation energy  sector when tesla entered china  u.s china they were really in the middle  of a trade war  so there was a huge incentive to  showcase  that china is opening to the world it's  not discriminating  against foreign investment it took tesla  less than a year to get its shanghai  plant up and running  that's half the time it took to launch  its battery producing gigafactory near  reno nevada  after getting funding from chinese banks  and quick approval from officials  tesla was delivering its first  chinese-made cars to local drivers by  early  2020  and in early 2021 tesla started  delivering its model y  cars car sales in china brought in more  than 6.6 billion dollars in revenue for  tesla in 2020  and helped the car maker reach a record  500 000 global vehicle deliveries that  year  but then in early 2021 chinese  regulators reported an  unusual uptick of customer complaints  about tesla quality issues  in this online video for example a tesla  driver appears to complain about the car  accelerating without the driver's foot  on the pedal  with cruise control and autopilot  functions appearing to be turned off  tesla didn't respond to a request for  comment on this video  authorities say they held talks with  tesla on the consumer reported abnormal  acceleration  and battery fires warning the car maker  that it needs to abide by chinese laws  and strengthen internal management to  ensure the quality and safety of its  products  it couldn't be determined whether the  cars and the videos circulating in china  were made in shanghai  the company said it would investigate  the claims and abide by the law  it didn't respond to our request for  comment  industry observers questioned whether  the speed at which tesla scaled up  production in china  could have affected the quality of its  cars tesla  was meeting a huge demand in china there  was also some  rush that might contribute to the  quality and may  now be able to provide quality products  in time to meet their demand tesla  didn't respond to our questions on  whether production speed may have  affected quality in china  but elon musk has acknowledged in a  recent interview that the company has  faced production challenges  during that like production ramp that's  it's super hard to  you know be like in vertical climb mode  and get everything right  industry analysts said tesla's response  to regulatory scrutiny in china  differs sharply from the tone it is  usually employed with regulators in the  u.s  in 2018 musk sparred with u.s regulators  as they investigated his tweets about  taking tesla private when his company  was in a cash crunch  tesla never ended up going private and  in 2020  musk initially defied a california  county government order to suspend  production due to coronavirus  and at one point he tweeted the  coronavirus panic is dumb  tesla's issues in china right now aren't  necessarily unique  other ev makers including its rival neo  have also reported battery fires  but transportation analysts say tesla  needs to protect its reputation in a  market that already represents 20  of its revenue and is expected to grow  i think that they has to be more careful  than chinese local  companies and they're bigger and they're  perceived to be  a better company tesla's been allowed to  operate with relative freedom  thanks to a loosening of china's rules  for foreign automakers in 2018.  for instance many foreign car makers  like gm and mercedes were required to  partner with local companies  but the silicon valley company faces  increased competition from local  startups including lee auto and  x-pang as it hopes to continue to gain  ground in china  pressure from regulators comes at a  critical time for tesla
 

